/>

<!-- 01 ANSWER-FIRST -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · The short answer</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">A no-drain Maytag is Whirlpool-platform parts — and the warranty won't cover it.</h2>

    <p><strong>Maytag washers are built on the Whirlpool platform, so a no-drain Maytag comes down to the same short list: a failed or clogged drain pump, a clog in the pump filter (coin trap) or drain hose, a kinked or too-deeply-inserted hose, or a stuck lid lock. On electronic models Maytag shows the F9E1 "long drain" code — the water didn't clear in time, which points at the pump or a clog, not the control. Here's the Maytag-specific catch: the famous 10-year limited warranty covers only the drive motor and wash basket (parts, not labor) — not the drain pump — so a no-drain repair generally isn't a warranty claim. Whether it's a Bravos top-loader or a Maxima front-loader, the drain system is identical. Clearing a hose or filter is homeowner-safe; the pump is a tech job. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair.</strong></p>

    <p class="callout"><strong>Won't drain, won't spin — same fault.</strong> A washer drains first, then spins. If it can't drain, it never reaches the spin step, so fix the drain and the spin usually returns.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 WARRANTY HONESTY -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · The 10-year warranty won't help here</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Maytag's warranty covers the motor and basket — not the pump.</h2>

    <p>Maytag markets a 10-year limited parts warranty, and it's real — but it's narrower than most people assume. On most models it covers only the <strong>drive motor</strong> and the <strong>wash basket</strong> (the stainless tub), and it's parts-only, not labor. The drain pump, the lid lock, the control board, and the hoses are <strong>not</strong> on that list.</p>

    <p>Since a washer that won't drain is almost always the pump or a clog, that repair generally falls outside the warranty. We're not saying that to discourage you — we're saying it so you're not surprised when the drain-pump repair isn't covered. We'll always check whether your specific fault and model qualify, but plan on a normal repair for a no-drain Maytag. For the full code list, see our <a href="/services/washer-repair/maytag-error-codes/">Maytag washer error codes</a> page.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 CAUSES -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · Why a Maytag won't drain</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">The causes, in the order our techs check them.</h2>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Kinked or misrouted drain hose (check first)</h3>
      <p>A kink behind the machine, or a hose shoved too far down the standpipe, stops or siphons the drain. The easiest thing to rule out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Clogged pump filter / coin trap (Maxima front-load)</h3>
      <p>Behind the bottom-front access panel on Maxima front-loaders. Coins and lint collect here — a common, safe DIY clear. Bravos top-loaders usually have no user filter.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Failed or blocked drain pump</h3>
      <p>If the hose and filter are clear, the pump can't move the water — worn out, or an item lodged in the impeller. A tech repair, and not warranty-covered.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>Stuck lid lock / door latch</h3>
      <p>Maytag washers won't run the drain or spin unless the lid locks. A failed lock reads as a no-drain, no-spin fault. Tech diagnosis.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 SAFE FIX -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">04 · What you can safely check</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Try these before it's a pump call.</h2>

    <ol class="diag-list">
      <li><strong>Unplug the washer first,</strong> and be ready for standing water when you open the filter or hose.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the drain hose</strong> for a kink, and make sure it's inserted only a few inches into the standpipe.</li>
      <li><strong>Clear the pump filter (coin trap)</strong> behind the bottom-front panel on a Maxima — towels down, shallow pan ready.</li>
      <li><strong>Run a drain/spin cycle</strong> to confirm — if the water clears and it spins, you're done.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="callout"><strong>Where to stop:</strong> the hose and pump filter are safe. Replacing the drain pump, freeing a lodged item, or a lid-lock/control fault are our techs' work — and the pump isn't warranty-covered, so expect a normal repair.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 SIBLING -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">05 · Same platform as Whirlpool and Amana</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">One drain system, several badges.</h2>

    <p>Because Maytag, Whirlpool, and Amana share the platform, the drain pump, coin trap, and F9E1 code work the same way across all of them — only the warranty terms and the badge differ. If your machine is actually a Whirlpool, the diagnosis is identical; see our <a href="/services/washer-repair/whirlpool-not-draining/">Whirlpool washer not draining</a> page. Our techs carry the common Whirlpool-platform pumps that fit the whole family, so a Maytag no-drain is usually a one-visit fix.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 06 TECH + LINKS -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">06 · When to call us</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Hose and filter clear, still won't drain? It's the pump.</h2>

    <p>When the drain hose is straight, the coin trap is clean, and the Maytag still won't drain, the fault is the pump or the lid lock — both tech repairs, and neither is warranty-covered. We test the pump, check for a lodged item, and confirm the lid lock, then get the drain (and the spin that follows it) working in one visit where possible.</p>

    <p>More help: the general <a href="/services/washer-repair/not-draining/">washer not draining</a> guide, the <a href="/services/washer-repair/wont-spin/">washer won't spin</a> page, and the <a href="/services/washer-repair/maytag-error-codes/">Maytag washer error codes</a> umbrella. Sibling brand: <a href="/services/washer-repair/whirlpool-not-draining/">Whirlpool not draining</a>. Same-day across <a href="/los-angeles/washer-repair/">Los Angeles</a>, <a href="/beverly-hills/washer-repair/">Beverly Hills</a>, and <a href="/pasadena/washer-repair/">Pasadena</a> in most cases. <a href="/book/">Book online</a> or call {phone}.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 07 FAQ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">07 · FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Maytag washer not draining: common questions.</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
